# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# One entry, and it names Qt rather than anything in this tree.
#
# QDBusMetaObject::createMetaObject keeps the meta-object it builds in a static
# hash for the life of the process: building one again is expensive, and a Qt
# process ends rather than unloading the cache. `notifyDesktop` asks for a single
# interface, so a widget test that finishes a run reports 181 bytes that belong to
# Qt's cache. The stack names the library, so a leak in the product still fails.
leak:QDBusMetaObject::createMetaObject
